From: RemoteOS maintainers <remoteos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] usbipd: restrict the raw export listener to IPv4 loopback

RemoteOS exposes USB devices only over its authenticated reverse TLS
relay. The raw USB/IP protocol has no authentication and must never
listen on a network-facing interface. A fixed IPv4 loopback address
keeps both the default and -4 paths local; -6 fails closed.

Upstream: Not submitted [appliance transport policy]

--- a/tools/usb/usbip/src/usbipd.c
+++ b/tools/usb/usbip/src/usbipd.c
@@ -52,10 +52,10 @@
 	"usage: usbipd [options]\n"
 	"\n"
 	"	-4, --ipv4\n"
-	"		Bind to IPv4. Default is both.\n"
+	"		Bind to IPv4 loopback (RemoteOS default).\n"
 	"\n"
 	"	-6, --ipv6\n"
-	"		Bind to IPv6. Default is both.\n"
+	"		IPv6-only mode is unsupported by RemoteOS and fails closed.\n"
 	"\n"
 	"	-e, --device\n"
 	"		Run in device mode.\n"
@@ -527,7 +527,10 @@
 	else
 		family = AF_INET6;
 
-	ai_head = do_getaddrinfo(NULL, family);
+	/* Raw USB/IP is accepted only from the authenticated local TLS relay.
+	 * Explicit IPv6-only mode fails closed rather than opening a public socket.
+	 */
+	ai_head = do_getaddrinfo("127.0.0.1", family);
 	if (!ai_head) {
 		usbip_driver_close(driver);
 		return -1;
